{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60106","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91162","text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-60107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91163","text":"OS-006 Governance Shim — authorization kernel for the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"id":"blk-60108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91164","text":"Issues signed, expiring "},{"id":"spn-91165","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorizationBlock"},{"id":"spn-91166","text":"s to destructive edges in OS-011 "},{"id":"spn-91167","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-91168","text":" replay flows. Policy-based, deny-by-default, pluggable policy store."}]},{"id":"blk-60109","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91169","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-60110","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91170","marks":["bold"],"text":"Library:"},{"id":"spn-91171","text":" v0.1.0 production-ready"}]}],"id":"blk-60111","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91172","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tests:"},{"id":"spn-91173","text":" 42/42 (25 unit + 3 integration + 14 MCP tool tests) + 2 body-os end-to-end integration tests"}]}],"id":"blk-60113","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91174","marks":["bold"],"text":"Storage:"},{"id":"spn-91175","text":" in-memory ETS-backed "},{"id":"spn-91176","marks":["code"],"text":"PolicyStore"},{"id":"spn-91177","text":" — Postgres-backed adapter is a future additive release"}]}],"id":"blk-60115","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60118","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91178","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP server:"},{"id":"spn-91179","text":" shipped — 6 tools on the "},{"id":"spn-91180","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"},{"id":"spn-91181","text":" namespace (put/get/list/delete policy + authorize + verify) with Anubis stdio/HTTP transport"}]}],"id":"blk-60117","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91182","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployment:"},{"id":"spn-91183","text":" "},{"id":"spn-91184","marks":["code"],"text":"fly.toml"},{"id":"spn-91185","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-91186","marks":["code"],"text":"Dockerfile"},{"id":"spn-91187","text":" ready for Fly.io ("},{"id":"spn-91188","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic-mcp"},{"id":"spn-91189","text":", port 4400)"}]}],"id":"blk-60119","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60121","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91190","text":"MCP surface"}]},{"id":"blk-60122","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"delegatic_put_policy       — register or replace a Policy\ndelegatic_get_policy       — look up a Policy by id\ndelegatic_list_policies    — list every registered Policy\ndelegatic_delete_policy    — remove a Policy\ndelegatic_authorize        — issue a fresh AuthorizationBlock\ndelegatic_verify           — verify a block's HMAC signature + TTL"},{"id":"blk-60123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91191","text":"Remote agents (body-browser-mcp, body-os-mcp, FleetPrompt's InstallEngine, Graphonomous replay flows) call "},{"id":"spn-91192","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic_authorize"},{"id":"spn-91193","text":" to obtain the fresh blocks they need for destructive edges per OS-011 §4.4."}]},{"id":"blk-60124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91194","text":"This is the "},{"id":"spn-91195","marks":["italic"],"text":"authorization kernel"},{"id":"spn-91196","text":" — the minimum needed to close the OS-011 destructive-edge loop. The full Delegatic spec ("},{"id":"spn-91197","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/"},{"id":"spn-91198","text":") layers on org trees, memberships, effective-policy computation, and a LiveView dashboard; those are future work."}]},{"id":"blk-60125","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91199","text":"Contract"}]},{"id":"blk-60126","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# 1. Register a policy\n:ok =\n  Delegatic.put_policy(\n    Delegatic.Policy.new(%{\n      policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n      allow_actions: [\"file_write\", \"shell_exec\"],\n      deny_actions: [\"file_delete\"],\n      agents: [\"ops-agent\"],\n      max_ttl_seconds: 300\n    })\n  )\n\n# 2. Directly request authorization for one action\n{:ok, block} =\n  Delegatic.authorize(\n    action_type: \"file_write\",\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\"\n  )\n\n# 3. Or build a function ready for the OS-011 Replay `:authorizer` slot\nauthorizer =\n  Delegatic.authorizer_for(\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\"\n  )\n\n# 4. Wire it into body-os replay\nBodyOs.Replay.execute(session, trace, authorizer: authorizer)"},{"id":"blk-60127","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91200","text":"AuthorizationBlock"}]},{"id":"blk-60128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91201","text":"Every issued block carries:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-60130","spans":[{"id":"spn-91202","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-60131","spans":[{"id":"spn-91203","text":"Example"}]}],"id":"blk-60129","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-60132","spans":[{"id":"spn-91204","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"}]},{"id":"blk-60133","spans":[{"id":"spn-91205","marks":["code"],"text":"\"delegatic://ws-42/ops\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-60134","spans":[{"id":"spn-91206","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_by"}]},{"id":"blk-60135","spans":[{"id":"spn-91207","marks":["code"],"text":"\"supervisor@acme\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-60136","spans":[{"id":"spn-91208","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_at"}]},{"id":"blk-60137","spans":[{"id":"spn-91209","text":"ISO8601 UTC"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60138","spans":[{"id":"spn-91210","marks":["code"],"text":"expires_at"}]},{"id":"blk-60139","spans":[{"id":"spn-91211","text":"ISO8601 UTC (capped at "},{"id":"spn-91212","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.max_ttl_seconds"},{"id":"spn-91213","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60140","spans":[{"id":"spn-91214","marks":["code"],"text":"authorization_token"}]},{"id":"blk-60141","spans":[{"id":"spn-91215","marks":["code"],"text":"\"sha256:<64-hex>\""},{"id":"spn-91216","text":" — HMAC over the other fields"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-60142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91217","text":"The token is "},{"id":"spn-91218","marks":["italic"],"text":"tamper-evident"},{"id":"spn-91219","text":", not secret — any consumer can call "},{"id":"spn-91220","marks":["code"],"text":"Delegatic.AuthorizationBlock.verify/1"},{"id":"spn-91221","text":" to detect forgery or expiration."}]},{"id":"blk-60143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91222","text":"The HMAC key lives in "},{"id":"spn-91223","marks":["code"],"text":"config :delegatic, :hmac_key"},{"id":"spn-91224","text":". A per-process random fallback is used when unset (fine for tests, unsafe for prod)."}]},{"id":"blk-60144","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91225","text":"Policy semantics"}]},{"id":"blk-60145","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91226","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action in deny_actions`"},{"id":"spn-91227","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-91228","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :denied_by_policy}"}]}],"id":"blk-60146","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91229","marks":["bold"],"text":"`agents` set and `agent_id` not in it"},{"id":"spn-91230","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-91231","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :agent_not_allowed}"}]}],"id":"blk-60148","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91232","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action not in allow_actions`"},{"id":"spn-91233","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-91234","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :not_in_allowlist}"},{"id":"spn-91235","text":" (deny-by-default)"}]}],"id":"blk-60150","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91236","text":"Otherwise → "},{"id":"spn-91237","marks":["code"],"text":":ok"}]}],"id":"blk-60152","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60154","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91238","text":"Wiring Delegatic into OS-011 replay"}]},{"id":"blk-60155","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91239","text":"The OS-011 spec §4.4 requires that every destructive replay edge obtain a "},{"id":"spn-91240","marks":["italic"],"text":"fresh"},{"id":"spn-91241","text":" authorization — prior authorization does not carry. Delegatic's "},{"id":"spn-91242","marks":["code"],"text":"authorizer_for/1"},{"id":"spn-91243","text":" returns a function that re-issues a new block on every call, producing exactly the semantics OS-011 demands:"}]},{"id":"blk-60156","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Recorded trace: destructive edges carry OLD authorization blocks\n# Replay stripper: body-os.Replay strips them before dispatch\n# Delegatic authorizer: fresh block for every edge that makes it through policy\n# Session: enforces the destructive-action gate on the fresh block"},{"id":"blk-60157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91244","text":"See "},{"id":"spn-91245","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/test/delegatic_integration_test.exs"},{"id":"spn-91246","text":" for the end-to-end test that exercises this flow — both the success path (allowlist policy → replay succeeds) and the failure path (readonly policy → replay halts with "},{"id":"spn-91247","marks":["code"],"text":"reason: \"authorization_failure\""},{"id":"spn-91248","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-60158","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91249","text":"Running the suite"}]},{"id":"blk-60159","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"mix deps.get\nmix test"},{"id":"blk-60160","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91250","text":"References"}]},{"id":"blk-60161","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91251","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-91252","text":" — full v0.2 spec (organizations, memberships, effective policy, dashboard)"}]}],"id":"blk-60162","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91253","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"},{"id":"spn-91254","text":" §4.4 — AuthorizationBlock contract"}]}],"id":"blk-60164","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91255","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/"},{"id":"spn-91256","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-91257","marks":["code"],"text":"body-browser/"},{"id":"spn-91258","text":" — OS-011 providers whose Replay flows consume Delegatic authorizers"}]}],"id":"blk-60166","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60168","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-91259","text":"License"}]},{"id":"blk-60169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-91260","text":"Apache-2.0"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawklv63ycvqvs6od7aj7lstiqvuuse4dcl7lbttxb6sgkay5n4rsa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}